    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it doesn't feel like \"growing\" though. it feels like being a stranger in my own life. everyone is just waiting for me to get better so things can go back to normal, but there is no normal. i'm just stuck in this loop of pretending to be human when i feel completely empty inside. it's just exhausting to keep performing.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's like you're trapped between being the person you used to be and the person you're trying to become, with everyone around you watching and expecting you to figure it out. The pressure to \"get better\" can be suffocating, and the constant need to perform can be exhausting. It might be time to redefine what \"normal\" means to you and find a way to break free from those expectations, even if that means being a stranger to yourself for a little while longer.",
